# Ghoroa — project context

## Phase 1 (signed agreement)

- Marketing website only: brand, menus, bilingual content, SEO.
- No cart, checkout, kitchen dashboard, or WooCommerce ordering.
- Operations (ordering/POS/KDS) = **Rosuii SaaS in Phase 2** — configured, not built here.

## The deliverable

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `ghoroa-web/` | **Production frontend** — Next.js App Router on Vercel |
| `ghoroa-core/` | Presence plugin — CPTs + public REST (`/ghoroa/v1`) |
| `ghoroa-theme/` | WordPress block theme — **non-production fallback** |
| `design/prototype-react/` | Design reference (Vite/React). **Never deployed.** |
| `design/prototype-static/` | Older static prototype. Reference only. |
| `docs/` | Scope, brand, contract |
| `docs/archive/ghoroa-core-commerce-superseded/` | Dead Woo code — **never reload** |

## Headless

- Content is edited in WordPress. Next fetches `/wp-json/ghoroa/v1/*`.
- Publish → Next `/api/revalidate` with signed secret.
- Locale routes: `/en` and `/bn`.
- Contact form on `/contact/` only (no cart, POS, or online ordering).

Content lives in the CMS, never hardcoded in templates. The client must be able to
change a price without a developer — that requirement outranks visual convenience.

## Locked IA (matches the signed agreement)

Nav: **Home · Menu · About · Locations · Contact**
Header button: **Order Now** → WhatsApp/phone now, Rosuii URL in Phase 2.
Footer: FAQ · Privacy · Terms + hours/phone/WhatsApp/socials.

Reservations is the enquiry form on `/contact/`, **not** a page. Online Order is a
CTA, **not** a page — the agreement says "No online ordering".

Stable URLs (Phase 2 depends on these): `/menu/`, `/about/`, `/contact/`,
`/locations/`, `/faq/`, `/privacy-policy/`, `/terms/`.

## Brand — `ghoroa-theme/theme.json` is the only token source

Ported from `design/prototype-react/` (forest/gold dark theme). **Never hardcode hex
elsewhere.**

- Fonts: Rottering (display) · Montserrat (body) · Hind Siliguri (BN), self-hosted.
- The site is **dark forest-based** (`#080d09` / `#062e1b`), not sand/rust.
- Accent is **terracotta red**: solid CTAs `terracotta #a13828` + cream text; on-dark
  text/outline accents use lighter reds (`#e07a68` / `#d46050`, still named `gold` /
  `gold-deep` in tokens for class compatibility). `parchment #F2E9DA` for light bands.
- `docs/brand/Ghoroa_Brand_Guidelines.html` (rust/sand) is print collateral — **not**
  the web palette. Numerals never use Rottering (no digit glyphs).

### Palette rules the contrast maths forces

- Raw `terracotta #a13828` is **not** AA as small text on dark — fills only (cream on top).
- Menu price leader uses `cream/15` on dark — decorative, not text.
- Parchment sections reset to `ink` / `muted` / `terracotta` via `.has-parchment-background-color`.
- Run `node ghoroa-theme/tools/check-contrast.mjs` after token changes.

## Checks — run both after touching the theme or plugin

```
php  ghoroa-core/tests/test-menu-list.php
node ghoroa-theme/tools/check-contrast.mjs
```

## Custom code budget

Exactly **one** custom block: `ghoroa/menu-list`, because core blocks cannot lay out
"name … leader … price" from post meta. Its editor UI is plain `wp.*` JS with no build
step — do not introduce a bundler into the plugin.

Everything else is core blocks, patterns, and `theme.json`. No page builders, no
Elementor, max 5–8 plugins.

## Logo

Approved marks under `ghoroa-theme/assets/images/ghoroa-logo*`.
**Do not invent or redesign logos.** Polish only, and only from an approved asset.

## Frontend UI components (ghoroa-web)

Use **Watermelon UI MCP only** for blocks/components/animated UI
(`search` → `get_component` → `npx shadcn add https://registry.watermelon.sh/r/…`).
Do not invent toggle/switch/accordion/nav chrome from scratch when a Watermelon
entry exists. Brand-adapt after install (forest/gold). shadcn MCP is disabled —
existing `src/components/ui/*` primitives stay; new interactive UI comes from Watermelon.
